    "metadata": {
      "title": "A Martin kernel with isolated Harnack contact in an annulus",
      "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23332261",
      "publication_date": "2026-10-12",
      "description": "<p>For the annulus 1 &lt; |z| &lt; e, with base point a = exp(1/2), the normalized minimal Martin kernel at the inner-boundary point -1 is strictly below the envelope of normalized positive harmonic functions throughout a punctured neighborhood of a. Four explicit positive harmonic competitors yield a uniform first-order gap in every direction. Direct Green-kernel construction and harmonic reflection establish the Martin limit and minimality.</p><p>This gives a negative answer to the equality-along-a-Green-line extension in Hayman and Lingham, Research Problems in Function Theory, arXiv:1809.07200v2, Problem 7.42, attributed to Arsove and Johnson. The statement concerns equality along a line issuing from the base point; it does not exclude isolated contact farther away. A dated, bounded priority audit accompanies the authored verification package. An addendum proves that a simpler punctured-disc counterexample is an elementary deduction from classical positive-harmonic representations, including Kohn (1966); this does not establish prior recognition of the Green-line consequence or yield the smooth-annulus theorem. No claim of first historical resolution or certification of current worldwide openness is made.</p><p>The deposit contains a concise research note and authored proof source, independent adversarial reviews and reproducibility materials. OpenAI tools were used extensively in solving, drafting and verifying the result. This is an unrefereed preprint, with no completed human peer review or formal proof-assistant certification claimed. Integrity checks and numerical checks do not replace the analytic proof.</p>",
      "access_right": "open",
      "creators": [
        {
          "name": "Kriebel, Alec",
          "affiliation": "Independent researcher",
          "orcid": "0009-0001-9320-500X"
        }
